cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SiCoPR — a Python port of the IEEE 802.3 COM MATLAB reference"
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below. It is
  an independent port and is not an IEEE deliverable; when the subject is the
  COM methodology itself rather than this implementation, cite the IEEE 802.3
  standard and the MATLAB reference instead.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bermensolo
    given-names: Todd
repository-code: "https://github.com/tbermen/SiCoPR"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
abstract: >-
  A function-for-function Python translation of the IEEE 802.3ck/dj Channel
  Operating Margin (COM) MATLAB reference tool, with R extensions for reports
  and visualisations. It computes COM, VEO and VEC and the supporting
  equalisation and noise analysis for a serial channel described by Touchstone
  S-parameter files and an Excel configuration spreadsheet. Against 208 MATLAB
  reference cases it chooses the same sampling phase and equalizer on every case
  and agrees on COM to 4.6e-14 dB; the scope and limits of that measurement are
  stated in the project README.
keywords:
  - channel operating margin
  - COM
  - IEEE 802.3
  - signal integrity
  - SerDes
  - equalization
license: BSD-3-Clause
references:
  - type: software
    title: "IEEE 802.3 Channel Operating Margin MATLAB reference implementation"
    authors:
      - name: "802-COM Authors"
    year: 2025
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >-
      The upstream this project translates. Redistributed unmodified under
      matlab/ with notices intact; exact versions and SHA-256 checksums are
      recorded in NOTICE. The MATLAB reference remains the normative
      implementation.
